+Microsoft build of Go 1.26 added a new `ms_version` setting. It controls whether
+the Go runtime uses a Microsoft-specific version string in the output of
+`runtime.Version()`. This in turn affects the output of `go version`.
+The possible values are:
+- "0": `runtime.Version()` returns the upstream version string, for example: "go1.26.0".
+- "1" (default): `runtime.Version()` returns the Microsoft build of Go version string, for example: "go1.26.0-1_microsoft".
